  "transcript": " The second reason is that products can get more complicated. This is not automatically bad. Useful features are useful. A safe replying is good. A better battery is good. A phone that survives gravity is basically a public service, but every extra feature is also one more thing that can break. A simple fridge has one main joe of be cold. Modern fridge may have screens, sensors, water lines, ice dispensers, software and opinions. At some point, the product is not just a product. It is a small technology committee living in your kitchen. And when one tiny part fails, the whole thing can become harder and more expensive to fix.",
